// Ch15 B10 "The dock-master" (C, 2 min). act2_ch15.md §2 B10, split out of ch15_current_song (that file is the open
// sea; this one is staged in Hollowmere). H04: Hollowmere at dawn, the first oil lamps on the hulls (rule 3 ends).
// H05: Aldous Varrow, the dock-master, at his hull-house door; he looks at the canopy, then at his daughter.
// H06: FROM THE BARGE, at a distance, Liss tells him. NO DIALOGUE IS HEARD in this beat: the errand is hers.
title: ch15_the_dock_master
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@letterbox on
@fade in 1.5
@camera H04
@wait 4.0
@camera H05
@mark aldous_varrow fathers_door walk
@anim aldous_varrow look_at tobin_bier
@wait 2.0
@anim aldous_varrow look_at liss
@wait 2.0
@camera H06
@mark liss fathers_door_liss walk
@wait 6.0
@anim aldous_varrow embrace liss
@wait 4.0
@music silence fade=3.0
<<set $ch15_liss_told_father = true>>
@letterbox off
@camera release
===
